<title>AUSTRALIA: ASC confirms Cultus Petroleum inquiry.</title>
<headline>ASC confirms Cultus Petroleum inquiry.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Securities Commission (ASC) confirmed on Monday it would inquire into Cultus Petroleum NL following a referral from the Australian Stock Exchange (ASX).</p>
<p>An ASC spokeswoman said the referral related to a &quot;matter of disclosure&quot; but would give no further details.</p>
<p>A number of newspapers said the ASX was inquiring into whether Cultus kept the market fully informed over the possible size of reserves in the Cornea oil field offshore Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Cultus shares were three cents lower at A$3.42 on Monday andt reached A$4.05 on May 29 when the Cornea report reached the market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
